language 0.1.0
module verification
  means
    Obtaining reproducible evidence that a statement is true or that a
    requirement is met.

entity verification : thing
  means
    verification: purposeful activity yielding evidence that a statement is
    true or that a requirement is met.

entity test : thing
  means
    test: an executable check of the behaviour of an object under given inputs
    and conditions.

entity test-case : thing
  means
    test case: a definite specification of the preconditions, inputs, actions
    and expected results of one trial.

entity proof : thing
  means
    proof: a finite justification that a statement follows from accepted
    axioms and rules of inference.

entity oracle : thing
  means
    oracle: a rule or mechanism determining the expected result of a test
    case.

entity evidence : thing
  means
    evidence: a retained result of a verification, confirming or refuting the
    statement under check.

entity coverage : thing
  means
    coverage: a measure of how much of an established set of objects or
    conditions the checks reach.

entity result : thing
  means
    result: the formalised outcome of a verification together with its status.
